From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] input-method-relay: raise the OSK on every output

When a layer surface (e.g. the lock screen) wants text input the OSK is
moved to the overlay layer so it isn't hidden. That only happened on the
layer surface's own output, but the OSK may be on another one (LG Wing:
keyboard on the swivel screen below the main screen).
---
--- a/src/input-method-relay.c	2026-11-16 04:04:19.984436257 +0400
+++ b/src/input-method-relay.c	2026-11-16 04:04:20.007468859 +0400
@@ -41,7 +41,9 @@
 static void
 elevate_osk (struct wlr_surface *surface)
 {
+  PhocDesktop *desktop = phoc_server_get_desktop (phoc_server_get_default ());
   struct wlr_layer_surface_v1 *layer;
+  PhocOutput *output;
 
   if (!surface)
     return;
@@ -50,7 +52,11 @@
   if (!layer)
     return;
 
-  phoc_layer_shell_update_osk (PHOC_OUTPUT (layer->output->data), TRUE);
+  /* The OSK can be on another output than the layer surface that wants
+   * input (e.g. a lock screen on the main screen and the OSK on a second
+   * built-in one) */
+  wl_list_for_each (output, &desktop->outputs, link)
+    phoc_layer_shell_update_osk (output, TRUE);
 }
 
 
